    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-legislation-amendment-emergencies-and-disasters-act-2006-sch-1-sec-80g",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "80G Interpretation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-legislation-amendment-emergencies-and-disasters-act-2006#sch-1-sec-80g"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-legislation-amendment-emergencies-and-disasters-act-2006.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-legislation-amendment-emergencies-and-disasters-act-2006.pdf, p.7",
      "values:originalText": "(1) In this Part:\nAustralian citizen has the same meaning as in the Australian\nCitizenship Act 1948.\nduty of confidence means any duty or obligation arising under the\ncommon law or at equity pursuant to which a person is obliged not\nto disclose information, but does not include legal professional\nprivilege.\nemergency declaration means a declaration under section 80J or\n80K.\npermanent resident means a person, other than an Australian\ncitizen:\n\n(a) whose normal place of residence is situated in Australia; and\n\n(b) whose presence in Australia is not subject to any limitation as\nto time imposed by law; and\n\n(c) who is not an illegal entrant within the meaning of the\nMigration Act 1958.\n\nSchedule 1  Privacy Act 1988\n\nsecrecy provision means a provision of a law of the\nCommonwealth, including a provision of this Act, that prohibits or\nregulates the use or disclosure of personal information, whether the\nprovision relates to the use or disclosure of personal information\ngenerally or in specified circumstances.\n\n(2) For the purposes of this Part, a reference in the definition of\npersonal information in subsection 6(1) to an individual is taken to\ninclude a reference to an individual who is not living.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) In this Part:\nAustralian citizen has the same meaning as in the Australian\nCitizenship Act 1948.\nduty of confidence means any duty or obligation arising under the\ncommon law or at equity pursuant to which a person is obliged not\nto disclose information, but does not include legal professional\nprivilege.\nemergency declaration means a declaration under section 80J or\n80K.\npermanent resident means a person, other than an Australian\ncitizen:\n\n(a) whose normal place of residence is situated in Australia; and\n\n(b) whose presence in Australia is not subject to any limitation as\nto time imposed by law; and\n\n(c) who is not an illegal entrant within the meaning of the\nMigration Act 1958.\n\nSchedule 1  Privacy Act 1988\n\nsecrecy provision means a provision of a law of the\nCommonwealth, including a provision of this Act, that prohibits or\nregulates the use or disclosure of personal information, whether the\nprovision relates to the use or disclosure of personal information\ngenerally or in specified circumstances.\n\n(2) For the purposes of this Part, a reference in the definition of\npersonal information in subsection 6(1) to an individual is taken to\ninclude a reference to an individual who is not living.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-legislation-amendment-emergencies-and-disasters-act-2006-sch-1-sec-80g-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-legislation-amendment-emergencies-and-disasters-act-2006-sch-1-sec-80g-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "91a0cb055f7bb22518572fd77275043d7ba96a2e5046cd1abd5dcf0c0f32b942"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-legislation-amendment-emergencies-and-disasters-act-2006#sch-1-sec-80g",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "80G Interpretation",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 7,
      "values:originalText": "(1) In this Part:\nAustralian citizen has the same meaning as in the Australian\nCitizenship Act 1948.\nduty of confidence means any duty or obligation arising under the\ncommon law or at equity pursuant to which a person is obliged not\nto disclose information, but does not include legal professional\nprivilege.\nemergency declaration means a declaration under section 80J or\n80K.\npermanent resident means a person, other than an Australian\ncitizen:\n\n(a) whose normal place of residence is situated in Australia; and\n\n(b) whose presence in Australia is not subject to any limitation as\nto time imposed by law; and\n\n(c) who is not an illegal entrant within the meaning of the\nMigration Act 1958.\n\nSchedule 1  Privacy Act 1988\n\nsecrecy provision means a provision of a law of the\nCommonwealth, including a provision of this Act, that prohibits or\nregulates the use or disclosure of personal information, whether the\nprovision relates to the use or disclosure of personal information\ngenerally or in specified circumstances.\n\n(2) For the purposes of this Part, a reference in the definition of\npersonal information in subsection 6(1) to an individual is taken to\ninclude a reference to an individual who is not living."
    },
