    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-legislation-amendment-emergencies-and-disasters-act-2006-sch-1-sec-80h",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "80H Meaning of permitted purpose",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-legislation-amendment-emergencies-and-disasters-act-2006#sch-1-sec-80h"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-legislation-amendment-emergencies-and-disasters-act-2006.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-legislation-amendment-emergencies-and-disasters-act-2006.pdf, p.8",
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Part, a permitted purpose is a purpose that\ndirectly relates to the Commonwealth’s response to an emergency\nor disaster in respect of which an emergency declaration is in force.\n\n(2) Without limiting subsection (1), any of the following is a permitted\npurpose in relation to an emergency or disaster:\n\n(a) identifying individuals who:\n\n(i) are or may be injured, missing or dead as a result of the\nemergency or disaster; or\n\n(ii) are or may be otherwise involved in the emergency or\ndisaster;\n\n(b) assisting individuals involved in the emergency or disaster to\nobtain services such as repatriation services, medical or other\ntreatment, health services and financial or other humanitarian\nassistance;\n\n(c) assisting with law enforcement in relation to the emergency\nor disaster;\n\n(d) coordination or management of the emergency or disaster;\n\n(e) ensuring that people who are responsible (within the\nmeaning of subclause 2.5 of Schedule 3) for individuals who\nare, or may be, involved in the emergency or disaster are\nappropriately informed of matters that are relevant to:\n\n(i) the involvement of those individuals in the emergency\nor disaster; or\n\n(ii) the response to the emergency or disaster in relation to\nthose individuals.\n\nPrivacy Act 1988  Schedule 1",
      "skos:definition": "(1) For the purposes of this Part, a permitted purpose is a purpose that\ndirectly relates to the Commonwealth’s response to an emergency\nor disaster in respect of which an emergency declaration is in force.\n\n(2) Without limiting subsection (1), any of the following is a permitted\npurpose in relation to an emergency or disaster:\n\n(a) identifying individuals who:\n\n(i) are or may be injured, missing or dead as a result of the\nemergency or disaster; or\n\n(ii) are or may be otherwise involved in the emergency or\ndisaster;\n\n(b) assisting individuals involved in the emergency or disaster to\nobtain services such as repatriation services, medical or other\ntreatment, health services and financial or other humanitarian\nassistance;\n\n(c) assisting with law enforcement in relation to the emergency\nor disaster;\n\n(d) coordination or management of the emergency or disaster;\n\n(e) ensuring that people who are responsible (within the\nmeaning of subclause 2.5 of Schedule 3) for individuals who\nare, or may be, involved in the emergency or disaster are\nappropriately informed of matters that are relevant to:\n\n(i) the involvement of those individuals in the emergency\nor disaster; or\n\n(ii) the response to the emergency or disaster in relation to\nthose individuals.\n\nPrivacy Act 1988  Schedule 1",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-legislation-amendment-emergencies-and-disasters-act-2006-sch-1-sec-80h-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-legislation-amendment-emergencies-and-disasters-act-2006-sch-1-sec-80h-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d13b4f57e3e8aa9bb4bfd904ea5e906b968114daa798b4d7178491ac8d46c8fa"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-legislation-amendment-emergencies-and-disasters-act-2006#sch-1-sec-80h",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "80H Meaning of permitted purpose",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 8,
      "values:originalText": "(1) For the purposes of this Part, a permitted purpose is a purpose that\ndirectly relates to the Commonwealth’s response to an emergency\nor disaster in respect of which an emergency declaration is in force.\n\n(2) Without limiting subsection (1), any of the following is a permitted\npurpose in relation to an emergency or disaster:\n\n(a) identifying individuals who:\n\n(i) are or may be injured, missing or dead as a result of the\nemergency or disaster; or\n\n(ii) are or may be otherwise involved in the emergency or\ndisaster;\n\n(b) assisting individuals involved in the emergency or disaster to\nobtain services such as repatriation services, medical or other\ntreatment, health services and financial or other humanitarian\nassistance;\n\n(c) assisting with law enforcement in relation to the emergency\nor disaster;\n\n(d) coordination or management of the emergency or disaster;\n\n(e) ensuring that people who are responsible (within the\nmeaning of subclause 2.5 of Schedule 3) for individuals who\nare, or may be, involved in the emergency or disaster are\nappropriately informed of matters that are relevant to:\n\n(i) the involvement of those individuals in the emergency\nor disaster; or\n\n(ii) the response to the emergency or disaster in relation to\nthose individuals.\n\nPrivacy Act 1988  Schedule 1"
    },
