    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-legislation-amendment-emergencies-and-disasters-act-2006-sch-1-sec-80k",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "80K Declaration of emergency—events outside Australia",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-legislation-amendment-emergencies-and-disasters-act-2006#sch-1-sec-80k"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-legislation-amendment-emergencies-and-disasters-act-2006.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-legislation-amendment-emergencies-and-disasters-act-2006.pdf, p.9",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Prime Minister or the Minister may make a declaration under\nthis section if the Prime Minister or the Minister (as the case may\nbe) is satisfied that:\n\n(a) an emergency or disaster has occurred outside Australia; and\n\n(b) the emergency or disaster is of such a kind that it is\nappropriate in the circumstances for this Part to apply in\nrelation to the emergency or disaster; and\n\n(c) the emergency or disaster has affected one or more\nAustralian citizens or permanent residents (whether within\nAustralia or overseas).\n\n(2) The Minister must consult the Minister administering the\nDiplomatic Privileges and Immunities Act 1967 before the Minister\nmakes a declaration under this section.\nNote:\nA declaration under this section is merely a trigger for the operation of\nthis Part and is not directly related to any other legislative or\nnon-legislative scheme about emergencies.\n\nSchedule 1  Privacy Act 1988",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Prime Minister or the Minister may make a declaration under\nthis section if the Prime Minister or the Minister (as the case may\nbe) is satisfied that:\n\n(a) an emergency or disaster has occurred outside Australia; and\n\n(b) the emergency or disaster is of such a kind that it is\nappropriate in the circumstances for this Part to apply in\nrelation to the emergency or disaster; and\n\n(c) the emergency or disaster has affected one or more\nAustralian citizens or permanent residents (whether within\nAustralia or overseas).\n\n(2) The Minister must consult the Minister administering the\nDiplomatic Privileges and Immunities Act 1967 before the Minister\nmakes a declaration under this section.\nNote:\nA declaration under this section is merely a trigger for the operation of\nthis Part and is not directly related to any other legislative or\nnon-legislative scheme about emergencies.\n\nSchedule 1  Privacy Act 1988",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-legislation-amendment-emergencies-and-disasters-act-2006-sch-1-sec-80k-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-legislation-amendment-emergencies-and-disasters-act-2006-sch-1-sec-80k-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3ee1e01efb07bfd2ae44111e6a10282825b43ab6a1df53f2de0788d1a9732822"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-legislation-amendment-emergencies-and-disasters-act-2006#sch-1-sec-80k",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "80K Declaration of emergency—events outside Australia",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 9,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Prime Minister or the Minister may make a declaration under\nthis section if the Prime Minister or the Minister (as the case may\nbe) is satisfied that:\n\n(a) an emergency or disaster has occurred outside Australia; and\n\n(b) the emergency or disaster is of such a kind that it is\nappropriate in the circumstances for this Part to apply in\nrelation to the emergency or disaster; and\n\n(c) the emergency or disaster has affected one or more\nAustralian citizens or permanent residents (whether within\nAustralia or overseas).\n\n(2) The Minister must consult the Minister administering the\nDiplomatic Privileges and Immunities Act 1967 before the Minister\nmakes a declaration under this section.\nNote:\nA declaration under this section is merely a trigger for the operation of\nthis Part and is not directly related to any other legislative or\nnon-legislative scheme about emergencies.\n\nSchedule 1  Privacy Act 1988"
    },
