      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Obligation",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Declaration obligation",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(c) the emergency or disaster has affected one or more Australian citizens or permanent residents (whether within Australia or overseas);",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The Prime Minister or the Minister may make a declaration under this section."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-legislation-amendment-emergencies-and-disasters-act-2006-sch-1-sec-80k-ss-1-logic-alleninterval-4",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:AllenInterval"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Between",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Declaration relates to events outside Australia",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::interval_reasoning",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(a) an emergency or disaster has occurred outside Australia;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The declaration applies to the emergency or disaster."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-legislation-amendment-emergencies-and-disasters-act-2006-sch-1-sec-80k-ss-1-logic-argumentation-5",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Argumentation"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Implication",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Declaration implies conditions for application",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::argumentation",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(b) the emergency or disaster is of such a kind that it is appropriate in the circumstances for this Part to apply in relation to the emergency or disaster;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The declaration applies if the condition is met."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-legislation-amendment-emergencies-and-disasters-act-2006-sch-1-sec-80k-ss-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "80K(2) Declaration of emergency—events outside Australia",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-legislation-amendment-emergencies-and-disasters-act-2006#sch-1-sec-80k-ss-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-legislation-amendment-emergencies-and-disasters-act-2006.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-legislation-amendment-emergencies-and-disasters-act-2006.pdf, p.9",
      "values:originalText": "(2) The Minister must consult the Minister administering the\nDiplomatic Privileges and Immunities Act 1967 before the Minister\nmakes a declaration under this section.\nNote:\nA declaration under this section is merely a trigger for the operation of\nthis Part and is not directly related to any other legislative or\nnon-legislative scheme about emergencies.\n\nSchedule 1  Privacy Act 1988",
      "skos:definition": "(2) The Minister must consult the Minister administering the\nDiplomatic Privileges and Immunities Act 1967 before the Minister\nmakes a declaration under this section.\nNote:\nA declaration under this section is merely a trigger for the operation of\nthis Part and is not directly related to any other legislative or\nnon-legislative scheme about emergencies.\n\nSchedule 1  Privacy Act 1988",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:privacy-legislation-amendment-emergencies-and-disasters-act-2006-sch-1-sec-80k"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
