    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-legislation-amendment-emergencies-and-disasters-act-2006-sch-1-sec-80k-ss-2-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Minister must consult other minister",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(2) The Minister must consult the Minister administering the Diplomatic Privileges and Immunities Act 1967 before the Minister makes a declaration under this section.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The Minister MUST consult the Minister administering the Diplomatic Privileges and Immunities Act 1967."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-legislation-amendment-emergencies-and-disasters-act-2006-sch-1-sec-80k-ss-2-logic-deontic-2",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Declaration is merely a trigger for the operation of this Part",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "A declaration under this section is merely a trigger for the operation of this Part and is not directly related to any other legislative or non-legislative scheme about emergencies.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "The Minister MUST declare that events outside Australia are occurring."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-legislation-amendment-emergencies-and-disasters-act-2006-sch-1-sec-80l",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "80L Form of declarations",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-legislation-amendment-emergencies-and-disasters-act-2006#sch-1-sec-80l"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-legislation-amendment-emergencies-and-disasters-act-2006.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-legislation-amendment-emergencies-and-disasters-act-2006.pdf, p.10",
      "values:originalText": "(1) An emergency declaration must be in writing and signed by:\n\n(a) if the Prime Minister makes the declaration—the Prime\nMinister; or\n\n(b) if the Minister makes the declaration—the Minister.\n\n(2) An emergency declaration must be published, as soon as\npracticable after the declaration has effect:\n\n(a) on the website maintained by the Department on the Internet;\nand\n\n(b) by notice published in the Gazette.\n\n(3) An emergency declaration is not a legislative instrument.\n80M  When declarations take effect\n\nAn emergency declaration has effect from the time at which the\ndeclaration is signed.\n80N  When declarations cease to have effect\n\nAn emergency declaration ceases to have effect at the earliest of:\n\n(a) if a time at which the declaration will cease to have effect is\nspecified in the declaration—at that time; or\n\n(b) the time at which the declaration is revoked; or\n\n(c) the end of 12 months starting when the declaration is made.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) An emergency declaration must be in writing and signed by:\n\n(a) if the Prime Minister makes the declaration—the Prime\nMinister; or\n\n(b) if the Minister makes the declaration—the Minister.\n\n(2) An emergency declaration must be published, as soon as\npracticable after the declaration has effect:\n\n(a) on the website maintained by the Department on the Internet;\nand\n\n(b) by notice published in the Gazette.\n\n(3) An emergency declaration is not a legislative instrument.\n80M  When declarations take effect\n\nAn emergency declaration has effect from the time at which the\ndeclaration is signed.\n80N  When declarations cease to have effect\n\nAn emergency declaration ceases to have effect at the earliest of:\n\n(a) if a time at which the declaration will cease to have effect is\nspecified in the declaration—at that time; or\n\n(b) the time at which the declaration is revoked; or\n\n(c) the end of 12 months starting when the declaration is made.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-legislation-amendment-emergencies-and-disasters-act-2006-sch-1-sec-80l-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-legislation-amendment-emergencies-and-disasters-act-2006-sch-1-sec-80l-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-legislation-amendment-emergencies-and-disasters-act-2006-sch-1-sec-80l-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "bdf4a828e9c304309781b33b947c93ff22de5f2e5bdf53562d5e62ce9c92c58a"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-legislation-amendment-emergencies-and-disasters-act-2006#sch-1-sec-80l",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "80L Form of declarations",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 10,
      "values:originalText": "(1) An emergency declaration must be in writing and signed by:\n\n(a) if the Prime Minister makes the declaration—the Prime\nMinister; or\n\n(b) if the Minister makes the declaration—the Minister.\n\n(2) An emergency declaration must be published, as soon as\npracticable after the declaration has effect:\n\n(a) on the website maintained by the Department on the Internet;\nand\n\n(b) by notice published in the Gazette.\n\n(3) An emergency declaration is not a legislative instrument.\n80M  When declarations take effect\n\nAn emergency declaration has effect from the time at which the\ndeclaration is signed.\n80N  When declarations cease to have effect\n\nAn emergency declaration ceases to have effect at the earliest of:\n\n(a) if a time at which the declaration will cease to have effect is\nspecified in the declaration—at that time; or\n\n(b) the time at which the declaration is revoked; or\n\n(c) the end of 12 months starting when the declaration is made."
    },
