      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Agency must authorize officer/employee actions.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Officer/employee authorized to collect, use and disclose personal information."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-legislation-amendment-emergencies-and-disasters-act-2006-sch-1-sec-80p-ss-7",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "80P(7) Authorisation of collection, use and disclosure of personal",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-legislation-amendment-emergencies-and-disasters-act-2006#sch-1-sec-80p-ss-7"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-legislation-amendment-emergencies-and-disasters-act-2006.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-legislation-amendment-emergencies-and-disasters-act-2006.pdf, p.10",
      "values:originalText": "(7) In this section:\ndesignated secrecy provision means any of the following:\n\n(a) sections 18 and 92 of the Australian Security Intelligence\nOrganisation Act 1979;\n\n(b) section 34 of the Inspector-General of Intelligence and\nSecurity Act 1986;\n\n(c) section 39, 39A, 40 and 41 of the Intelligence Services Act\n2001;\n\n(d) a provision of a law of the Commonwealth prescribed by the\nregulations for the purposes of this paragraph;\n\n(e) a provision of a law of the Commonwealth of a kind\nprescribed by the regulations for the purposes of this\nparagraph.\nentity includes the following:\n\n(a) a person;\n\n(b) an agency;\n\n(c) an organisation.",
      "skos:definition": "(7) In this section:\ndesignated secrecy provision means any of the following:\n\n(a) sections 18 and 92 of the Australian Security Intelligence\nOrganisation Act 1979;\n\n(b) section 34 of the Inspector-General of Intelligence and\nSecurity Act 1986;\n\n(c) section 39, 39A, 40 and 41 of the Intelligence Services Act\n2001;\n\n(d) a provision of a law of the Commonwealth prescribed by the\nregulations for the purposes of this paragraph;\n\n(e) a provision of a law of the Commonwealth of a kind\nprescribed by the regulations for the purposes of this\nparagraph.\nentity includes the following:\n\n(a) a person;\n\n(b) an agency;\n\n(c) an organisation.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:privacy-legislation-amendment-emergencies-and-disasters-act-2006-sch-1-sec-80p"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
