    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-legislation-amendment-emergencies-and-disasters-act-2006-sch-1-sec-80q",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "80Q Disclosure of information—offence",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-legislation-amendment-emergencies-and-disasters-act-2006#sch-1-sec-80q"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-legislation-amendment-emergencies-and-disasters-act-2006.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-legislation-amendment-emergencies-and-disasters-act-2006.pdf, p.12",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person (the first person) commits an offence if:\n\n(a) personal information that relates to an individual is disclosed\nto the first person because of the operation of this Part; and\n\n(b) the first person subsequently discloses the personal\ninformation; and\n\nPrivacy Act 1988  Schedule 1\n\n(c) the first person is not responsible for the individual (within\nthe meaning of subclause 2.5 of Schedule 3).\nPenalty: 60 penalty units or imprisonment for 1 year, or both.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply to the following disclosures:\n\n(a) if the first person is an agency—a disclosure permitted under\nan Information Privacy Principle;\n\n(b) if the first person is an organisation—a disclosure permitted\nunder an approved privacy code or a National Privacy\nPrinciple;\n\n(c) a disclosure permitted under section 80P;\n\n(d) a disclosure made with the consent of the individual to whom\nthe personal information relates;\n\n(e) a disclosure to the individual to whom the personal\ninformation relates;\n\n(f) a disclosure to a court;\n\n(g) a disclosure prescribed by the regulations.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to a matter in\nsubsection (2) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code).\n\n(3) If a disclosure of personal information is covered by\nsubsection (2), the disclosure is authorised by this section.\n\n(4) For the purposes of paragraph (2)(f), court includes any tribunal,\nauthority or person having power to require the production of\ndocuments or the answering of questions.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person (the first person) commits an offence if:\n\n(a) personal information that relates to an individual is disclosed\nto the first person because of the operation of this Part; and\n\n(b) the first person subsequently discloses the personal\ninformation; and\n\nPrivacy Act 1988  Schedule 1\n\n(c) the first person is not responsible for the individual (within\nthe meaning of subclause 2.5 of Schedule 3).\nPenalty: 60 penalty units or imprisonment for 1 year, or both.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply to the following disclosures:\n\n(a) if the first person is an agency—a disclosure permitted under\nan Information Privacy Principle;\n\n(b) if the first person is an organisation—a disclosure permitted\nunder an approved privacy code or a National Privacy\nPrinciple;\n\n(c) a disclosure permitted under section 80P;\n\n(d) a disclosure made with the consent of the individual to whom\nthe personal information relates;\n\n(e) a disclosure to the individual to whom the personal\ninformation relates;\n\n(f) a disclosure to a court;\n\n(g) a disclosure prescribed by the regulations.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to a matter in\nsubsection (2) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code).\n\n(3) If a disclosure of personal information is covered by\nsubsection (2), the disclosure is authorised by this section.\n\n(4) For the purposes of paragraph (2)(f), court includes any tribunal,\nauthority or person having power to require the production of\ndocuments or the answering of questions.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-legislation-amendment-emergencies-and-disasters-act-2006-sch-1-sec-80q-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-legislation-amendment-emergencies-and-disasters-act-2006-sch-1-sec-80q-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-legislation-amendment-emergencies-and-disasters-act-2006-sch-1-sec-80q-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-legislation-amendment-emergencies-and-disasters-act-2006-sch-1-sec-80q-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1b89b457d1bb5d34f7f6a06701c1c45cf46cb9474dbdd62d91203f20681c3900"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-legislation-amendment-emergencies-and-disasters-act-2006#sch-1-sec-80q",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "80Q Disclosure of information—offence",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 12,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person (the first person) commits an offence if:\n\n(a) personal information that relates to an individual is disclosed\nto the first person because of the operation of this Part; and\n\n(b) the first person subsequently discloses the personal\ninformation; and\n\nPrivacy Act 1988  Schedule 1\n\n(c) the first person is not responsible for the individual (within\nthe meaning of subclause 2.5 of Schedule 3).\nPenalty: 60 penalty units or imprisonment for 1 year, or both.\n\n(2) Subsection (1) does not apply to the following disclosures:\n\n(a) if the first person is an agency—a disclosure permitted under\nan Information Privacy Principle;\n\n(b) if the first person is an organisation—a disclosure permitted\nunder an approved privacy code or a National Privacy\nPrinciple;\n\n(c) a disclosure permitted under section 80P;\n\n(d) a disclosure made with the consent of the individual to whom\nthe personal information relates;\n\n(e) a disclosure to the individual to whom the personal\ninformation relates;\n\n(f) a disclosure to a court;\n\n(g) a disclosure prescribed by the regulations.\nNote:\nA defendant bears an evidential burden in relation to a matter in\nsubsection (2) (see subsection 13.3(3) of the Criminal Code).\n\n(3) If a disclosure of personal information is covered by\nsubsection (2), the disclosure is authorised by this section.\n\n(4) For the purposes of paragraph (2)(f), court includes any tribunal,\nauthority or person having power to require the production of\ndocuments or the answering of questions."
    },
