    {
      "@id": "concept:privacy-legislation-amendment-emergencies-and-disasters-act-2006-sch-1-sec-80t",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "80T Compensation for acquisition of property—constitutional safety",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-legislation-amendment-emergencies-and-disasters-act-2006#sch-1-sec-80t"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "privacy-legislation-amendment-emergencies-and-disasters-act-2006.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "privacy-legislation-amendment-emergencies-and-disasters-act-2006.pdf, p.15",
      "values:originalText": "net\n\n(1) If the operation of this Part would result in an acquisition of\nproperty from a person otherwise than on just terms, the\nCommonwealth is liable to pay a reasonable amount of\ncompensation to the person.\n\n(2) If the Commonwealth and the person do not agree on the amount\nof the compensation, the person may institute proceedings in a\ncourt of competent jurisdiction for the recovery from the\nCommonwealth of such reasonable amount of compensation as the\ncourt determines.\n\n(3) In this section:\nacquisition of property has the same meaning as in paragraph\n51(xxxi) of the Constitution.\njust terms has the same meaning as in paragraph 51(xxxi) of the\nConstitution.\n\nSchedule 2  Australian Security Intelligence Organisation Act 1979",
      "skos:definition": "net\n\n(1) If the operation of this Part would result in an acquisition of\nproperty from a person otherwise than on just terms, the\nCommonwealth is liable to pay a reasonable amount of\ncompensation to the person.\n\n(2) If the Commonwealth and the person do not agree on the amount\nof the compensation, the person may institute proceedings in a\ncourt of competent jurisdiction for the recovery from the\nCommonwealth of such reasonable amount of compensation as the\ncourt determines.\n\n(3) In this section:\nacquisition of property has the same meaning as in paragraph\n51(xxxi) of the Constitution.\njust terms has the same meaning as in paragraph 51(xxxi) of the\nConstitution.\n\nSchedule 2  Australian Security Intelligence Organisation Act 1979",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-legislation-amendment-emergencies-and-disasters-act-2006-sch-1-sec-80t-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-legislation-amendment-emergencies-and-disasters-act-2006-sch-1-sec-80t-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:privacy-legislation-amendment-emergencies-and-disasters-act-2006-sch-1-sec-80t-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a08a0fcbdeafd3c1b3a4b495b9a9c9d96850f08946b52bc0622347d3b6e73b78"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/privacy-legislation-amendment-emergencies-and-disasters-act-2006#sch-1-sec-80t",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "80T Compensation for acquisition of property—constitutional safety",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 15,
      "values:originalText": "net\n\n(1) If the operation of this Part would result in an acquisition of\nproperty from a person otherwise than on just terms, the\nCommonwealth is liable to pay a reasonable amount of\ncompensation to the person.\n\n(2) If the Commonwealth and the person do not agree on the amount\nof the compensation, the person may institute proceedings in a\ncourt of competent jurisdiction for the recovery from the\nCommonwealth of such reasonable amount of compensation as the\ncourt determines.\n\n(3) In this section:\nacquisition of property has the same meaning as in paragraph\n51(xxxi) of the Constitution.\njust terms has the same meaning as in paragraph 51(xxxi) of the\nConstitution.\n\nSchedule 2  Australian Security Intelligence Organisation Act 1979"
    },
